-- title:
--   Grouping frozen bundle remainders into proper-face cut tests
-- statement:
--   A selected nonempty occurrence edge is enumerated by its ordered projected base face. The bundle supplies the corresponding occurrence-vertex and tuple equivalences.
--
--   For each remainder edge after erasing a maximum-cardinality edge, a selected vertex omitted by that remainder is chosen and converted to its canonical coordinate. The missing-vertex choice is totalized outside the used remainder edges by an arbitrary vertex of the selected edge.
--
--   Insertion reconstructs a selected-edge tuple from an erased coordinate and a filler value, then combines it with frozen outside variables. Grouping each remainder factor by its chosen missing coordinate gives the deleted-coordinate cut-test family. Factors remain indexed by occurrence edges, so repeated projected base faces remain separate contributions.
